      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T02:23:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 326: 🟡 `natPmpCtx` and its runner are created unconditionally, even when `HAVE_LIBNATPMP` is disabled. That adds an idle io_context thread in builds that cannot use NAT-PMP. Consider guarding the member initialization/runner creation behind `HAVE_LIBNATPMP`, or only creating the dedicated context when the NAT-PMP protocol is actually registered.",
      "revId": "841268add1fd7055092b81b7cfac037c62e9b7ea",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b70ad1f5_ec079d4d",
        "filename": "include/upnp/upnp_context.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 365,
      "author": {
        "id": 1035
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-11T14:44:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This comment is irrelevant and appears to be based on a misunderstanding of the purpose of `igdDiscoveryTimeout_`. The \"IGD discovery phase\" was added in https://review.jami.net/c/dhtnet/+/28903 as an optimization, to make mappings fail faster in the case where there is no IGD. The timeout does not make it impossible to detect a working IGD; it just means that some mapping requests may fail while we\u0027re in the process of discovering and setting up the IGD.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 360,
